1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:02,615
Kewalram Chanrai Group.

2
00:00:02,745 --> 00:00:05,257
EJO 100, Enterprise Platform.

3
00:00:05,387 --> 00:00:06,805
Built by JusTech.

4
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:12,070
This is EJO 100: one platform for the
whole group,

5
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,327
from the front desk to the boardroom.

6
00:00:14,457 --> 00:00:17,620
Every member of staff signs in with their
own account,

7
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:19,877
and sees only what their role allows.

8
00:00:20,007 --> 00:00:23,049
Let's start where the day starts, at the
front desk.

9
00:00:24,679 --> 00:00:26,831
The dashboard is the morning briefing.

10
00:00:26,961 --> 00:00:31,035
Live counts of the vehicles in the
workshop, jobs waiting on approval,

11
00:00:31,165 --> 00:00:35,358
parts that need reordering, and everything
that changed since yesterday.

12
00:00:35,488 --> 00:00:37,760
While a page loads, the EJO mark pulses,

13
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:40,703
so you always know the system is working
for you.

14
00:00:42,912 --> 00:00:44,589
Customers live in one place.

15
00:00:44,719 --> 00:00:48,461
A profile holds the vehicles, every job
card, every payment,

16
00:00:48,591 --> 00:00:51,106
and the full history of the relationship.

17
00:00:51,236 --> 00:00:56,010
Nothing is typed twice, and nothing is
lost when a member of staff moves on.

18
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:59,667
The workshop runs on job cards.

19
00:00:59,797 --> 00:01:05,512
A job card follows a vehicle from gate to
gate: intake, inspection, estimate, parts,

20
00:01:05,642 --> 00:01:07,739
work done, billing, and release.

21
00:01:07,869 --> 00:01:10,453
Every step records who did it and when,

22
00:01:10,583 --> 00:01:14,976
so a supervisor can see the state of the
whole floor at a glance.

23
00:01:16,606 --> 00:01:19,560
Every document prints on the group's own
letterhead.

24
00:01:19,690 --> 00:01:24,305
The logo sits beside the wordmark, the
green rule carries the group name beneath

25
00:01:24,435 --> 00:01:24,483
it,

26
00:01:24,613 --> 00:01:27,093
and the executing branch follows
underneath,

27
00:01:27,223 --> 00:01:30,593
exactly as on the printed job card the
workshop uses today.

28
00:01:32,639 --> 00:01:35,898
Inventory knows every part on the shelf:
what is in stock,

29
00:01:36,028 --> 00:01:40,455
what is reserved against a job card, what
has just arrived on a goods receipt,

30
00:01:40,585 --> 00:01:43,026
and what has fallen below its reorder
level.

31
00:01:43,156 --> 00:01:46,707
The store manager sees the numbers before
the shelf runs empty.

32
00:01:48,337 --> 00:01:51,011
Approvals route themselves to the right
person.

33
00:01:51,141 --> 00:01:54,709
A supervisor approves first, the manager
gives the final word,

34
00:01:54,839 --> 00:01:58,228
and the rules make sure nobody signs off
their own request.

35
00:01:58,358 --> 00:02:02,642
Each decision is one tap, and the
requester is told the moment it happens.

36
00:02:04,272 --> 00:02:06,620
At the gate, security registers visitors,

37
00:02:06,750 --> 00:02:09,218
logs every vehicle coming in and going
out,

38
00:02:09,348 --> 00:02:13,750
and issues exit passes and road test
passes that print with a reference the

39
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:14,717
gate can verify.

40
00:02:14,847 --> 00:02:18,282
Who is on the premises right now is always
one screen away.

41
00:02:21,139 --> 00:02:23,046
The schedule brings meetings, rooms,

42
00:02:23,176 --> 00:02:26,723
visitors and appointments into one
calendar for the whole branch.

43
00:02:26,853 --> 00:02:30,401
Book a room, invite colleagues, and the
gate knows who to expect.

44
00:02:35,439 --> 00:02:37,638
Customer care runs the support centre.

45
00:02:37,768 --> 00:02:42,173
Every request becomes a ticket with an
owner, a deadline, and a follow-up.

46
00:02:42,303 --> 00:02:46,401
Service hours and teams are set by the
business, not by the software.

47
00:02:48,031 --> 00:02:50,767
Enyo is the assistant built into the
platform.

48
00:02:50,897 --> 00:02:55,065
Ask it in plain language and it answers
from the group's own records,

49
00:02:55,195 --> 00:02:57,993
with the same permissions as the person
asking.

50
00:02:58,123 --> 00:03:02,603
It summarises, drafts, and explains, and
it never sees data it should not.

51
00:03:04,233 --> 00:03:08,448
Leadership sees across every branch:
workflow analytics, headquarters

52
00:03:08,578 --> 00:03:09,141
dashboards,

53
00:03:09,271 --> 00:03:11,534
and a complete, append-only audit log.

54
00:03:11,664 --> 00:03:15,690
Every action in the system can be traced
to a person and a moment,

55
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:18,649
which is what makes the numbers worth
trusting.

56
00:03:20,279 --> 00:03:21,871
And it all fits in a pocket.

57
00:03:22,001 --> 00:03:27,035
EJO 100 installs on any phone like an app,
with the same data, the same permissions,

58
00:03:27,165 --> 00:03:30,539
and the same letterhead, wherever the work
happens to be.

59
00:03:36,579 --> 00:03:38,936
EJO 100, Enterprise Platform.

60
00:03:39,066 --> 00:03:43,567
Built by Just Technologies for Kewalram
Chanrai Group.

61
00:03:43,697 --> 00:03:45,196
Powered by EJO 100.
